# Ash Ledger has no environment variables today.
#
# The entire app is a static, client-side calculator: every number a viewer
# sees is computed in their own browser from the values they type into the
# Input Console. There is no API, no database, and no secret to protect, so
# there is nothing to put in this file — it exists only so the project has
# the usual place to add one later.
#
# If you extend the app with a backend (e.g. a Vercel Serverless/Edge
# Function to save named scenarios, or an API route that emails a PDF of the
# current view), add real entries here, then:
#   1. Prefix anything the BROWSER bundle needs to read with VITE_ — Vite
#      only inlines env vars with that prefix (e.g. VITE_API_BASE_URL).
#   2. Leave server-only secrets (API keys, DB URLs) WITHOUT the VITE_
#      prefix so they are never bundled into client-side JavaScript.
#   3. Set the real values in Vercel: Project -> Settings -> Environment
#      Variables (see README.md "Deploying to Vercel" for the walkthrough).
#
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=
